    ["位置2-洛耀"] = "Position 2 - Luo Yao",
    ["你一觉醒来，却成了另一个人——霍伊大学历史系毕业生，有一个哥哥和一个妹妹，口袋里只剩几枚便士。这算什么？一场离奇的梦，还是命运开的一个玩笑？\n\n穿越，这是克莱恩给自己的第一个答案。\n他以为这只是一次意外的偏离，以为只要找到回家的路，就能回到原来曾经的家，回到那个不需要扮演任何人的世界。于是他小心翼翼地披上“克莱恩”的外壳，学习非凡，总结扮演法则，从泛黄的典籍里试着拼凑出一条归乡的路。\n\n可故事并未朝着他所期待的方向发展。长辈失控，队长牺牲，身不由己地卷入了一场与己无关的巨大阴谋。他死过一次，又从深渊的边缘死而复生。当他再度睁开眼时，发现自己早已不再是这个世界的过客，那些真实存在过的温暖与记忆，已经成了他维系人性、不可或缺的锚点。\n\n只是，现在的它们都被无情地碾碎了。于是他暂时收起“回家”的执念，走上另一条路——复仇。不再徘徊，不再犹豫。他开始谋划，开始变强，戴上小丑的面具，在灰雾之上以“愚者”之名俯瞰众生。\n“总有一天，我会回去的。”他低声说，“但不是现在。”\n还有太多账没有算清，太多人还没等到迟来的审判。回家，似乎成了一个遥远而漫长的目标。\n“但幸运的是，我是一个有耐心的人。”\n\n灰雾之上，“愚者”先生缓缓睁开了眼睛。 "] = "You wake up, but you have become someone else—a history graduate of Khoy University, with an older brother and a younger sister, and only a few pence left in your pocket. What is this? A bizarre dream, or a joke played by fate? \n \n Transmigration, this is the first answer Klein gave himself. \n He thought it was just an accidental deviation, thinking that as long as he found the way home, he could return to his former home, to the world where he didn’t need to act as anyone. So he carefully put on the shell of “Klein,” learned about Beyonders, summarized the acting principles, and tried to piece together a way home from the yellowed classics. \n \n But the story did not develop in the direction he expected. The elder lost control, the captain sacrificed, and he was involuntarily involved in a huge conspiracy that had nothing to do with him. He died once, and died and resurrected from the edge of the abyss. When he opened his eyes again, he found that he was no longer a passerby in this world, and those warm memories that had truly existed had become the anchors he needed to maintain his humanity. \n \n It’s just that they have all been ruthlessly crushed now. So he temporarily put away the obsession of “going home” and embarked on another path—revenge. No more wandering, no more hesitation. He began to plan, began to become stronger, put on the mask of a clown, and overlooked all living beings above the gray fog in the name of “The Fool.” \n “One day, I will go back.” He whispered, “But not now.” \n There are too many accounts that have not been settled, and too many people who have not waited for the late judgment. Going home seems to have become a distant and long goal. \n “But fortunately, I am a patient person.” \n \n Above the gray fog, Mr. “The Fool” slowly opened his eyes.",
